        "required_age": 0,
        "is_free": false,
        "controller_support": "full",
        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3675290/extras/9656a4e462a948cf04bdd4a89cfa4509.avif?t=1763982876\" width=616 height=98 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Crystal Gaiden Origins</strong> is a side-scrolling action platformer with a bold 8-bit aesthetic, pulsing chiptunes, and razor-sharp gameplay.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Play as a rogue warrior fighting through burning cities, buried ruins, high-tech research facilities, and an active orbital elevator primed to unleash a doomsday weapon — all in a collapsing sci-fi world.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tear through rebel strongholds with advanced weaponry, and strike down your former brothers in the imperial army using forbidden powers buried in the past — all while uncovering a conspiracy that threatens the one you love. Trigger a berserk system that boosts your strength at the cost of your own health — every strike a sacrifice to bring her back.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A tribute to the 80s–90s era of NES action platformers — from Ninja Gaiden and Shatterhand to Castlevania and Shadow of the Ninja.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >8-bit graphics</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Side-scrolling Action Platformer</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sharp controls</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >6 levels</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >5 Sub Weapons</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >20+ types of enemies</p></li></ul>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3675290/extras/9656a4e462a948cf04bdd4a89cfa4509.avif?t=1763982876\" width=616 height=98 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Crystal Gaiden Origins</strong> is a side-scrolling action platformer with a bold 8-bit aesthetic, pulsing chiptunes, and razor-sharp gameplay.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Play as a rogue warrior fighting through burning cities, buried ruins, high-tech research facilities, and an active orbital elevator primed to unleash a doomsday weapon — all in a collapsing sci-fi world.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tear through rebel strongholds with advanced weaponry, and strike down your former brothers in the imperial army using forbidden powers buried in the past — all while uncovering a conspiracy that threatens the one you love. Trigger a berserk system that boosts your strength at the cost of your own health — every strike a sacrifice to bring her back.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A tribute to the 80s–90s era of NES action platformers — from Ninja Gaiden and Shatterhand to Castlevania and Shadow of the Ninja.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >8-bit graphics</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Side-scrolling Action Platformer</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sharp controls</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >6 levels</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >5 Sub Weapons</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >20+ types of enemies</p></li></ul>",
        "short_description": "Crystal Gaiden Origins is a hardcore 8-bit action platformer inspired by the brutal edge of NES-era classics. Slash through rebels, ex-allies, dark ancient technology, and a crumbling empire in chiptune-fueled missions. Inspired by Ninja Gaiden, Shatterhand, and Castlevania.",
        "supported_languages": "English, Simplified Chinese, French, Spanish - Spain, Japanese, Portuguese - Brazil, Portuguese - Portugal, Spanish - Latin America, Traditional Chinese, Russian",
        "reviews": "“An 8 bit action game straight from the glorious era of NES”<br>Mardax Games<br><br>“If you’re ready for a tough, old-school ride through a dark sci-fi world, keep this one on your radar.”<br>GameStick<br><br>“Love Letter to NES Action Platformers!”<br>NicoPlaysIndies<br>",
